[b]Star Adventurers[/b]
[list]
[*] 1.	Star Adventurers can be acquired after Difficult Mode is unlocked;
[*] 2.	Star Adventurers have a chance of spawn whenever an ancient Adventurer is generated:
[list]
[*] a.	Summon has 10% chance;
[*] b.	Adventurer pack has 20% chance;
[*] c.	Completing difficult dungeons has 30% chance;
[*] d.	Completing Mystic Dimension dungeons has 50% chance;
[*] e.	Inn routine refresh has 50% chance;
[*] f.	Town events have 60% chance.
[/list]
[*] 3.	Star Adventurers have significantly higher growth potential, with maximum rating of 404;
[*] 4.	Each Star Adventurer has unique Star Effect.
[/list]

[b]Item Update[/b]
[list]
[*] 1.	5 new scrolls and 2 new star effects are added, and star effects have a chance to be generated from items of level 8 and higher. 
[/list]

[b]Asset Update[/b]
[list]
[*] 1.	We have updated all battle maps😊
[/list]

[b]Other changes[/b]
[list]
[*] 1.	Increased damage cap to 500 million;
[*] 2.	Increased output capacity cap to 50 million;
[*] 3.	Adjusted recipe display in armour and weapon shops: recipes of level 8 and above will have their version of least P level shown;
[*] 4.	Fixed possible deadlock bugs associated with revive effects;
[*] 5.	Fixed a bug preventing Missionary’s dispels not properly trigger Collection Devices;
[*] 6.	Other minor bug fixes;
[/list]

Happy gaming everyone!

[h1]New Equipment Type: Device[/h1]

[list]
    [*]Devices are dropped from high level dungeons in Normal Mode, and all dungeon levels in Hard Mode;
    [*]Devices can automatically collect and release energies, provide significant battle advantages;
    [*]Devices can be re-forged and enchanted.
[/list]

[h1]Furnace Enhanced: Gems Combine[/h1]

[list]
    [*]Every 3 gems of the same type and level can be combined, to create a higher-level version gem of the same type.
    [*]Gem level cap is now 25.
[/list]


[h1]Other Changes[/h1]

[list]
    [*]All consumables are no longer counted as ‘item’: they will not occupy inventory space and cannot be sold;
    [*]Players can now sort items by effects in inventory filter;
    [*]Auto-tactic policy now unlocks at town title level 5;
    [*]Effect Immunity bug fix: effects that cannot be immuned are now properly honored;
    [*]Fixed a bug that caused auto-tactic does not process ‘free cast’ tactics while in Cooling Down state;
    [*]Added team number display in adventurer panel;
    [*]Optimized game save and backup process;
    [*]Other minor bug fixes.
[/list]


Finally, we are currently working in full swing on a Dragon Cliff project and will be able to make more detailed announcements in coming months. Being the first game for two of us, Dragon Cliff has received tremendous supports from community. We cherish this opportunity and will make our best efforts to push this title further.
Happy gaming everyone!

[h1]New Difficulty Setting Feature [/h1]
1.	Added new difficulty setting, now when player has completed quest ‘demon dragon’ in normal mode, hard mode is enabled, and switching difficulty setting can be done in ‘profile selector’.
2.	Each difficulty level has its own progress record;
3.	Normal mode levels may drop up to level 8 gears, and level 7 gems;
4.	Hard mode levels may drop up to level 10 gears, and level 9 gems;
5.	Drop rate of star items and newly added ‘fragment of demon’ is 2000% in hard mode levels than in normal mode levels;
6.	Exploration, production and furnace combine are not impacted by difficulty setting;
7.	Newly added ‘Remnants’ quest bosses are guaranteed to drop 1 star-quality accessory in hard mode; 


[h1]Itemization Update[/h1]
1.	Added unique star effects for Fame, Lightning Runner, Dragon Seal, Warm Jade, Clear Water, Phoenix, Soul Seal, and Insolence;
2.	Star accessories can only be dropped from bosses of newly added quest ‘Remnants’.
3.	Gems and socket patches now have reasonable sell prices;
4.	Chests no longer drop accessories;
5.	Dungeons no longer drop socket patches, and instead, they are regular commodities in shop;
6.	Life potions are now regular commodities in shop and no longer have grades;
7.	Excessed healings generated by life potions are converted into absorb shields, and this effect may not be dispelled.
8.	Simplified socket rule: removed limitation of 2 maximum manual socket (via patch) per item. Now all weapons can have a maximum of 4 sockets, and all armors can have a maximum of 3 sockets.
9.	Socket patches are stacked in inventory;


[h1]New Enchanting Feature[/h1]
1.	Ancient weapons and armors can be enchanted in Furnace;
2.	Normal ancient items may have 1 additional enchanted property, and star items may have 2 such properties;
3.	Enchanting lv.8+ items will need ‘fragment of demon’.
4.	Fragment of Demon can be found in all bosses (last 49 levels in normal mode, and all levels in hard mode) with very limited drop rate. Bosses of ‘Remnants’ always drop fragments of demon.


[h1]Integrated Achievement System[/h1]
1.	All achievements that have already been met with relevant requirements are automatically collected during session startup;


[h1]New Random Quest ‘Remnants’[/h1]
1.	When town title is at or above ‘Wonderful Future’ in either difficulty setting, it is possible to trigger random quest ‘Remnants’ upon completing any dungeon levels.
2.	‘Remnants’ expires after 15 days, and defeating the final boss will be rewarded with multiple ancients, possible star accessory (guaranteed in hard mode), and fragments of demon;


[h1]Additional Adjustments[/h1]
1.	Cap for money and practice points has been decreased to 50000000;
2.	Cost for item combine now is a flat fee of 100000 for all lv.8+ items, regardless of quality;
3.	Decreased residency expansion cost for early game;
4.	Increased resident limit to 25;
5.	Adjusted resident spawn mechanic: the quality of resident spawn is no longer directly linked to recently completed dungeon level, instead, player’s best achieved dungeon level will always be used for determining resident quality;
6.	Fixed an error of weapon special effect: x% chance of dealing y% damage to all enemy;
7.	Now all high difficulty dungeon levels will have 60% speed penalty for all units, increased from 40%;
8.	Adjusted ‘Harmony’ skill: now increases primary attribute of caster (changed from intelligence).
9.	Added multiple adventure team edit feature;
10.	Added attack descriptions for all monsters, you can view them by mouse over icons next to monsters’ health bar;
11.	Removed ‘build’ functions, buildings will be automatically constructed when relevant permit is acquired.

[h1] New contents [/h1]

1.	Added new quest chain: Princess of Lu. Quest can be triggered if main quest ‘Bone Demon’ has been completed.

2.	Added new quest: Evil Books. Quest can be triggered if you have completed ‘Demon Dragon 2’.

3.	Added new quest: Exploration. Quest can be triggered when town title is at or above ‘Salvation of Heaven’.

4.	Added new ‘Exploration’ feature, you can send out adventurers and residents for exploration, collecting resources and gears.

5.	Added 5 new town titles.

6.	Adventurers’ level cap is increased to 90;

7.	Added ‘Summon’ feature for inn: spend practice points to instantly summon a new adventurer;

8.	Added new accessory ‘Warm Jade’, available in all levels;

9.	Added level 8+ version of all existing accessories;

[h1]Adjustments[/h1]

1.	All tank adventurers now benefit 25% more from vitality attribute. (Increased from 1 vitality to 4 maximum health points, to 1 vitality to 5 maximum health points)

2.	All balanced adventurers now benefit 12.5% more from vitality attribute. (Increased from 1 vitality to 4 maximum health points, to 1 vitality to 4.5 maximum health points)

3.	Life on Hit is now capped to recover a maximum of 20% of caster’s maximum health.

4.	Only healers can generate critical heals, and all the other types of heals (life on hit, potions, per turn, per battle, etc.) can no longer crit.

5.	Adjusted armors’ attribute potentials;

6.	Adjusted weapons’ attribute potentials;

7.	All level 8+ weapon/armor recipes without extra properties are removed;

8.	Adjusted Missionary’s skills: 
‘Pray’now has 50% chance of removing 1 negative effect from target(s); 
‘Spell of Holiness’ now removes 4 negative effects at level 2, and 6 at level 3;

9.	Adjusted Night-blade’s skills:
‘Poisons Mist’ now lasts 6 seconds instead of 3 turns;

10.	Adjusted Warrior’s skills:
‘Sunder’ now reduces all resistances from targets, and reduction value on level 2 is 1000 (increased from 700), and 2000 (increased from 1000) on level 3;

11.	Adjusted Tough Woman’s skills:
‘Swift Wind’ now increases speed by 900 (increased from 600) at level 2, and 1500(increased from 900) at level 3;

12.	Adjusted Bun Sister’s skills:
‘Punishment’ now deals 80/100/120% real damage, and cooling down is reduced to 1 second;

13.	Fixed a bug where Bun Sister’s Bright Circle skill is not properly buffing all resistances;

14.	Adjusted Golden Shaman’s skills:
‘Divine Remedy’ cooling down is reduced to 1 second;

15.	Increased adventurers’ upgrade card re-roll cost cap;

16.	Stun units can no longer perform turns;

17.	Added detailed information for strength, intelligence, vitality, and resistances in Adventurer Panel;

18.	Upgraded save backup strategy: every 15 game days, system will automatically backup a game save file, up to 10 most recent backups. This should take care of most scenarios that may result in save file corruption/loss.

19.	Other minor bug fixes;

1.	Fixed auto-sell lag issue;

2.	Increased production boost cap to 5000%, and magic find cap to 3000%;

3.	Fixed lag issues caused by certain skills/items/special effects, and we are still working on rolling out more optimizations in future updates;

4.	Significantly boosted gem patch drop rate again, now in Hellish Path, the drop rate is 10%+, and in all 2-star levels is 20%+, it is also possible to have multiple drops from a single boss kill.

5.	Significantly boosted Tactician’s invitation drop rate from level 31 and above in Imperial Mausoleum;

6.	Increased materials drop rate and quantity in all 2-star levels;

7.	Now weapon and armor default craft volume is increased to 999;

8.	Users can now right click on recipe to auto-craft the highest possible volume of selected gear, without the need to click ‘craft’ again.

9.	Start Adventure Panel’s adventurer list is now sorted by levels.

10.	Added ‘Default’ sort in inventory, to avoid unequipped items getting auto-sorted.

11.	Adjusted effects of Boss Bird Monster in Imperial Mausoleum: decreased ‘Inversed Mandate’ charge rate, damage rate and stun seconds; Removed its ‘Swift’ passive.

12.	Minor bug fixes.

In the next few days we may push through more optimization updates to address lag issues in battle. We won’t be posting announcements for them as they can get repetitive. We will make more noises again when our new town expansion upgrade goes live, which should be within a week!

1. Added low level material drops for 2 star dungeons;

2. Removed money cost for craft items;

3. Increased drop rate for gem batch on 2 star levels;

4. Minor bug fixes 

We are currently working on town system expansion, and once the update goes live, there will be more ways to collect game money:)

Thanks!

